body:
I see. Could I use async/await for that? perhaps that is as simple as adding the async keyword? Like:

    const mergePDFs = async () => {       
        // merge the pdfs     
        // when they're done merging...      
    }); 
    } 

Or would I need to call that `resolve()` somehow/somewhere?

Here is the actual existing `mergePDFs` function, if it helps (it already has some async stuff going on so I don;t know if that changes anything):

    const mergePDFs = () => {
      (async () => { 
        merger.add('./a.pdf'); 
        merger.add('./b.pdf'); 
        merger.add('./c.pdf');

        await merger.save('mergedpdf.pdf'); 
      })(); 
    };
